        "original_id": "e04d39c6-fe22-54e9-9998-bf71faa5fb7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Quality Cafe, Los Angeles, California, 1236 West 7th Street\n- Products: Old School, Training Day, Se7en, Ghost World, Gone in 60 Seconds, The Stepfather, What's Love Got to Do with It, Sex and Death 101, Catch Me If You Can\n- Companies: DreamWorks Pictures, The Montecito Picture Company\n- People: Todd Phillips\n- Topics: diners, film locations\n\nFacts:\n- Quality Cafe, also known as Quality Diner, was a diner at 1236 West 7th Street in Los Angeles, California.\n- Old School is a 2003 American comedy film released by DreamWorks Pictures and The Montecito Picture Company and directed by Todd Phillips.\n- In late 2006, Quality Cafe ceased to operate as a diner.\n- After closing as a diner, Quality Cafe was used as a filming location for Hollywood films including Training Day, Old School, Se7en, Ghost World, Gone in 60 Seconds, The Stepfather, What's Love Got to Do with It, Sex and Death 101, and Catch Me If You Can.",
